From 48c3c37a2914c33b189d7dbbd0ee2ddae50f142e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI-Lab <mia.ailab1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 16:39:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 20/25] contract: GLM's three E4M3 latent launches on KV pages
 record their compiles

tf_glm_lat_write_fp8_paged, tf_glm_chunks_16_fp8_paged and tf_glm_chunks_32_fp8_paged are registered as their
window twins are launched: glm_glue, 512 and 256 threads, the chunks' 83,328 and 101,120 opt-in dynamic bytes, sm_80
on. nvcc 13.0's receipts are owed (usage none, so 13.0 images stay pending); nvcc 13.3's five-SM usage is in
measurements/pending_133.zig, read from a -Dsm=80,86,89,120,121 glm_glue fatbin of this tree with the contract's own
cubin reader (the same registers, static bytes and bounds kernel-contract-limits prints; its window twins read back
exactly as their records at the stock kernels):

  lat_write_fp8_paged  30 30 30 27 27 registers, 64 static bytes, bound 512
  chunks_16_fp8_paged  178 178 128 128 128, bound 256
  chunks_32_fp8_paged  218 218 196 159 159, bound 256

Every one fits every SM's limits. A test holds each paged launch to its twin's image, block, shared bytes and bound,
and the registry to exactly these three paged FP8 launches.

